Hello, I am currently trying to fit a Structural Equation Model using lavaan to data that I have simulated, and am having issues with model convergence. I have attached a png of the path diagram for the model to this discussion. Forgive me if it is slightly hard to read, I was not very familiar with the software I used to generate it. My goal in fitting this model is to estimate the factor loading matrices. I want to accurately estimate the factor loading matrices (which are known as I use them to simulate the data), and to do so, I impose several constraints such that there is no indeterminancy (rotational, scalar, or otherwise). The constraints, as seen in the path diagram, are as follows:<div><br></div><div>1. For the factor loadings between my observed independent covariates (X1-X20) and the latent factors from which they are generated (W1-W3), I have fixed the factor loadings for X1~W1, X2~W2, and X3~W3 at 1, and the factor loadings for X1~W2, X1~W3, and X2~W3 at 0.</div><div><br></div><div><div>2. For the factor loadings between my observed dependent covariates (Y1-Y20) and the latent factors from which they are generated (Z1-Z2), I have fixed the factor loadings for Y1~Z1, and Y2~Z2 at 1, and the factor loading for Y1~Z2 at 0.</div><div><br></div></div><div>3. The 3 latent factors W1, W2, and W3 have variance 1, and all 3 are mutually independent.</div><div><br></div><div>To the best of my knowledge, these should be sufficient conditions such that the remaining (unfixed) factor loadings between (X1-X20) and (W1-W3), (Y1-Y20) and (Z1-Z2), and coefficient matrix containing the regression estimates of (Z1-Z2) on (W1-W3) can all be uniquely estimated. Of course, the true factor loadings and covariance matrix of (W1-W3) are correspondingly fixed at these values. The covariance matrices of the error terms (which are simply the identity matrix) should be estimable as well, though these are not of particular interest currently. However, when I try and fit this model as I have defined it in lavaan, I receive a warning message from the optimizer stating that a solution has not been found, and correspondingly, the estimated factor loadings and regression coefficients are quite inaccurate. I have found that when I fix a single one of the regression coefficients of (Z1-Z2) on (W1-W3) at the truth (it does not seem to matter which coefficient I choose), I receive no warnings or errors when fitting the model, and the estimated factor loadings and regression coefficients are accurate. Is anyone able to help me figure out why these issues are arising when fitting the model? I have also included below the R code I have used to define and fit my model. Please let me know if any further clarifications are desired. Thank you very much for the assistance.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div><br></div><div>Alexander</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>library(lavaan)<br></div><div>library(stringr)<br></div><div><br></div><div>datgen &lt;- function(ak, bk, gamma, n,varvecB,varvecA,varvecG){<br>  if((is.atomic(gamma)) &amp; (length(gamma) == 1L)){<br>    W &lt;- matrix(rnorm(n, mean = 0, sd = 1), nrow = 1, n)<br>  }<br>  else{<br>    W &lt;- matrix(rnorm(n*ncol(gamma), mean = 0, sd = 1), nrow = ncol(gamma), n) ## generate matrix U N(0,I) m x n<br>  }<br>  xlin.term  &lt;-  bk %*% rbind(rep(1, ncol(W)),W)<br>  xlin.term &lt;- t(xlin.term)<br>  xx &lt;- matrix(0, nrow = n, ncol = nrow(bk))<br>  for(jj in 1: (ncol(xx))){<br>    xx[, jj] &lt;- xlin.term[,jj] + cbind(rnorm(n, mean = 0, sd = sqrt(varvecB[jj])))<br>  }<br>  colnames(xlin.term) &lt;- paste0(&#39;X&#39;, 1:(ncol(xx)))<br>  colnames(xx) &lt;- paste0(&#39;X&#39;, 1:(ncol(xx)))<br>  X = xx<br> <br>  if((is.atomic(gamma)) &amp; (length(gamma) == 1L)){<br>    Z &lt;- gamma*W + matrix(rnorm(n, mean = 0, sqrt(varvecG)), nrow = 1) ## generate latent matrix Z<br>  }<br>  else{<br>    Z &lt;- matrix(0, nrow=nrow(gamma), ncol = n)<br>    for(i in 1:nrow(gamma)){<br>      Z[i,] &lt;- gamma[i,]%*%W + matrix(rnorm(n, mean = 0, sd = sqrt(varvecG[i])), nrow = 1) ## generate latent matrix Z<br>    }<br>  }<br>  ylin.term  &lt;-  ak %*% rbind(rep(1, ncol(Z)),Z)<br>  ylin.term &lt;- t(ylin.term)<br>  yy &lt;- matrix(0, nrow = n, ncol = nrow(ak))<br>  for(jj in 1: (ncol(yy))){<br>    yy[, jj] &lt;- ylin.term[,jj] + cbind(rnorm(n, mean = 0, sd = sqrt(varvecA[jj])))<br>  }<br>  colnames(ylin.term) &lt;- paste0(&#39;Y&#39;, 1:(ncol(yy)))<br>  colnames(yy) &lt;- paste0(&#39;Y&#39;, 1:(ncol(yy)))<br>  Y = yy<br>  output &lt;- list(&quot;X&quot; = X, &quot;Y&quot; = Y, &quot;Z&quot; = Z)<br>}<br><br>set.seed(2435)<br><br>paramsA0 &lt;- rnorm(20)<br>paramsB0 &lt;- rnorm(20)<br>paramsB &lt;- matrix(c(1, -0.65, 0.65, rep(0.8,7), rep(0.70, 10), 0, 1, 0.70, rep(-0.85, 7), rep(-0.75, 10), 0, 0, 1, rep(0.55, 7), rep(-0.85, 10)), nrow = 20, ncol = 3)<br>paramsA &lt;- matrix(c(1, 0.45, -0.80, rep(0.80, 7), rep(-0.45, 10), 0, 1, 0.70, rep(0.40, 7), rep(-0.95, 10)), nrow = 20, ncol = 2)<br>paramsG &lt;- matrix(c(0.60, -0.75, -0.70, 0.65, 0.80, -0.55), nrow = 2, ncol = 3)<br>q &lt;- 20<br>p &lt;- 20<br>s &lt;- 3<br>m &lt;- 2<br><br>paramsAstotal &lt;- cbind(paramsA0, paramsA)<br>paramsBstotal &lt;- cbind(paramsB0, paramsB)<br><br>varvecB &lt;- rep(1,20)<br>varvecA &lt;- rep(1,20)<br>varvecG &lt;- rep(1,m)<br><br>set.seed(1)<br><br>dat &lt;- datgen(paramsAstotal, paramsBstotal, paramsG, 200, varvecB, varvecA, varvecG)<br><br>colnames(dat$X) &lt;- sprintf(&quot;X%d&quot;, 1:q)<br>colnames(dat$Y) &lt;- sprintf(&quot;Y%d&quot;, 1:p)<br><br>mydat &lt;- cbind(dat$X, dat$Y)<br><br>X1vals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, 1:q, 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, 1:q, 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>X2vals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, (q+1):(2*q), 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, (q+1):(2*q), 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>X3vals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, (2*q+1):(3*q), 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;x%d*X%d +&quot;, (2*q+1):(3*q), 1:q), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>Y1vals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;y%d*Y%d +&quot;, 1:p, 1:p), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;y%d*Y%d +&quot;, 1:p, 1:p), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>Y2vals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;y%d*Y%d +&quot;, (p+1):(2*p), 1:p), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;y%d*Y%d +&quot;, (p+1):(2*p), 1:p), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>Wvals &lt;- substr(paste(sprintf(&quot;w%d*W%d +&quot;, 1:s, 1:s), collapse = &#39; &#39;), 1 ,nchar(paste(sprintf(&quot;w%d*W%d +&quot;, 1:s, 1:s), collapse = &#39; &#39;))  - 2)<br>X1model &lt;- paste(paste0(sprintf(&quot;W%d =~ &quot;, 1), X1vals), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>X2model &lt;- paste(paste0(sprintf(&quot;W%d =~ &quot;, 2), X2vals), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>X3model &lt;- paste(paste0(sprintf(&quot;W%d =~ &quot;, 3), X3vals), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>Y1model &lt;- paste(paste0(sprintf(&quot;Z%d =~ &quot;, 1), Y1vals), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>Y2model &lt;- paste(paste0(sprintf(&quot;Z%d =~ &quot;, 2), Y2vals), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>Xmodel &lt;- c(X1model, X2model, X3model)<br>Ymodel &lt;- c(Y1model, Y2model)<br>Wvar &lt;- paste(sprintf(&quot;W%d ~~ 1*W%d&quot;, 1:s, 1:s), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>Wcov &lt;- c()<br><br>k &lt;- 1<br><br>for(i in 1:s){<br>  Xmodel[i] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;x&quot;, i+q*(i-1), &quot;[*]X&quot;, i, &quot; &quot;), paste0(&quot;1*X&quot;, i, &quot; &quot;), Xmodel[i])<br>  for(j in 1:s){<br>    if(i &lt; j){<br>      Wcov[k] &lt;- paste(sprintf(&quot;W%d ~~ 0*W%d&quot;, i, j), sep = &#39;
&#39;)<br>      k &lt;- k+1<br>    }<br>  }<br>}<br>Xmodel[2] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;x21&quot;), paste0(&quot;0&quot;), Xmodel[2])<br>Xmodel[3] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;x41&quot;), paste0(&quot;0&quot;), Xmodel[3])<br>Xmodel[3] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;x42&quot;), paste0(&quot;0&quot;), Xmodel[3])</div><div><br>for(i in 1:m){<br>  Ymodel[i] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;y&quot;, i+p*(i-1), &quot;[*]Y&quot;, i, &quot; &quot;), paste0(&quot;1*Y&quot;, i, &quot; &quot;), Ymodel[i])<br>}<br>Ymodel[2] &lt;- gsub(paste0(&quot;y21&quot;), paste0(&quot;0&quot;), Ymodel[2])<br>Zmodel &lt;- c(&quot;Z1 ~ W1 + W2 + W3&quot;, &quot;Z2 ~ W1 + W2 + W3&quot;)<br><br></div><div>#below is code where 1 of the regression coefficients is fixed at the truth</div><div>#Zmodel &lt;- c(&quot;Z1 ~ W1 + W2 + W3&quot;, &quot;Z2 ~ W1 + W2 + -0.55*W3&quot;)<br><br>mymodel &lt;- c(Xmodel, Ymodel, Zmodel, Wvar, Wcov)<br>lav_mod &lt;- sem(mymodel, data = mydat, meanstructure = T)</div>
